# 3. Category Normalization & Resolution

RSS/API sources can provide different category names for the same type of content.

For example:

```text
Political News
Politics
Political
Opinion
```

These should not create separate categories in the PulseVow database.

The ingestion pipeline maps external categories to a controlled set of canonical PulseVow categories.

```text
RSS Feed
   │
   │ category = "Political News"
   ▼
NormalizerService
   │
   │ slugify()
   │ "political-news"
   ▼
CATEGORY_MAP
   │
   │ "political-news" → "politics"
   ▼
NormalizedArticle
   │
   │ categorySlug = "politics"
   ▼
ArticleService
   │
   │ connect({ slug: "politics" })
   ▼
Category table
   │
   │ politics exists ✅
   ▼
Article created ✅
```

### Category normalization

The raw RSS category is converted into a slug:

```ts
const rawCategorySlug = slugify(categoryName, {
  lower: true,
  strict: true,
});
```

The normalized slug is then mapped to a canonical PulseVow category:

```ts
const categorySlug =
  CATEGORY_MAP[rawCategorySlug] ?? "general";
```

### Example mapping

```text
RSS Category          PulseVow Category
-----------------------------------------
Political News   →    politics
Political        →    politics
Politics         →    politics
Opinion          →    politics

Business         →    business
Economy          →    business
Markets          →    business
Finance          →    business

Technology       →    technology
Tech             →    technology
Gadgets          →    technology

Sports           →    sports
Sport            →    sports

Entertainment    →    entertainment
Movies           →    entertainment
Cinema           →    entertainment

World            →    world
International    →    world

Science          →    science

India            →    general
National         →    general
Unknown          →    general
```

### Canonical PulseVow Categories

The `Category` table should contain the controlled categories:

```text
General
Politics
Business
Technology
Sports
Entertainment
World
Science
```

Each category should have a unique slug:

```text
General          → general
Politics         → politics
Business         → business
Technology       → technology
Sports           → sports
Entertainment    → entertainment
World            → world
Science          → science
```

### Article-to-Category connection

The article is connected using the canonical category slug:

```ts
category: {
  connect: {
    slug: article.categorySlug,
  },
},
```

The `ArticleService` does not create arbitrary categories from RSS input.

This ensures that the database contains a controlled taxonomy and prevents RSS publishers from creating categories such as:

```text
Latest
Featured
Breaking
National
India
Top Stories
Editor's Pick
```

