# 8. Headline Tone

Headline Tone measures how emotionally charged, subjective, sensational, or urgent a headline is.

## Headline Tone Score

```text
Headline Tone Score =
    Emotional Intensity × 0.30
  + Subjectivity        × 0.25
  + Sensationalism      × 0.25
  + Urgency             × 0.10
  + Sentiment Intensity × 0.10
```

The final score is normalized to:

```text
0–100
```

### Headline Tone Classification

|  Score | Label   | Meaning                                             |
| -----: | ------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
|   0–20 | Neutral | Factual, straightforward headline                   |
|  21–40 | Mild    | Slightly expressive but mostly factual              |
|  41–60 | Charged | Noticeable emotional/opinionated wording            |
|  61–80 | Strong  | Highly emotional, dramatic or persuasive            |
| 81–100 | Extreme | Very sensational, provocative or emotionally loaded |

